From 2d5a929567a26f277541d965422034aaf6266afa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 10:00:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] fix(styles): keep the stylesheet inside the odontogram

The shipped stylesheet styled the host page: html/body/* rules, a global
select style, an !important .hidden class and eight short theme variables on
:root (--bg, --card, --accent, ...) that host design systems also use.

- page-level rules move to the demo (src/demo.css)
- the short theme variables become private (--_odon-*); --odon-* is unchanged
- the hide utility becomes .odon-hidden (all toggle sites and tests)
- tools/postcss-scope.js scopes every selector to .odontogram-root and the
  engine's odon-* popups with a zero-specificity :where(); the perio info
  popover gains an odon-popover class
- dist/style.layer.css: the same rules in @layer odontogram for hosts that
  use cascade layers

Tests: stylesheet-scope.test.ts; existing card/UI tests updated for
.odon-hidden.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LCyGZy1hJThR67oFx5pzCS
