+### Changed
+
+- **The stylesheet no longer styles the host page.** `dist/style.css` used to
+  ship `html`/`body`/`*` rules, a global `select` style, an `!important`
+  `.hidden` class and eight short theme variables on `:root` (`--bg`, `--card`,
+  `--muted`, `--accent`, `--line`, `--text`, `--panel`, `--accent2`) — names a
+  host design system is likely to use for something else. Now:
+  - the page-level rules live in the demo only (`src/demo.css`);
+  - the short variables are private (`--_odon-bg`, `--_odon-card`, …); the
+    public `--odon-*` theme variables are unchanged;
+  - the hide utility is `.odon-hidden` (every toggle site and test updated);
+  - `tools/postcss-scope.js` appends a zero-specificity
+    `:where(.odontogram-root, .odontogram-root *, [class*="odon-"], [class*="odon-"] *)`
+    to every selector at build time, so `.btn`, `.card`, `.row`, `select`… only
+    match inside the component or the engine's own `odon-*` popups (the perio
+    info popover gained an `odon-popover` class for this). The library's own
+    cascade is unchanged.
+
+### Added
+
+- **`react-advanced-odontogram/style.layer.css`** — the same stylesheet inside
+  `@layer odontogram`, for hosts that order their CSS with cascade layers
+  (Tailwind CSS 4 and others): unlayered CSS would otherwise beat every layered
+  utility of the host.
+
